//
// Secrets.example.xcconfig — committed template.
//
// Copy this file to Config/Secrets.xcconfig (git-ignored) and fill in your
// own credentials. The app builds without it — cloud providers then show
// "not configured" until keys are supplied.
//
//   cp Config/Secrets.example.xcconfig Config/Secrets.xcconfig
//
// Dropbox: create an app at https://www.dropbox.com/developers/apps
//   (Scoped access; redirect URI hellonotes://dropbox-auth). PKCE — key only.
// Box: create a Custom App (User Authentication / OAuth 2.0) at
//   https://app.box.com/developers/console (redirect URI hellonotes://box-auth).
//   Box's token exchange requires the client secret.
//

// Google Drive: create a project at https://console.cloud.google.com, enable
//   the Google Drive API, configure the OAuth consent screen (add yourself as a
//   test user if External), and create an OAuth client ID of type "iOS" with
//   this app's bundle id. PKCE — client id only; the redirect URI derives from
//   the reversed client id automatically.
//

// OneDrive: register an app at https://entra.microsoft.com (App registrations).
//   Account types "Multitenant + personal accounts" (covers Business AND
//   Personal), platform "Public client/native (mobile & desktop)", redirect URI
//   hellonotes://onedrive-auth, Authentication → Allow public client flows = Yes,
//   API permissions → Microsoft Graph delegated Files.ReadWrite + offline_access.
//   PKCE — client id only.
//

DROPBOX_APP_KEY =

BOX_CLIENT_ID =
BOX_CLIENT_SECRET =

GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID =

ONEDRIVE_CLIENT_ID =
